 "rules": {
  "consistency_gate": "the 36 M1 capture readouts bitwise (runner); every donor's new capture readout equals M1's; otherwise INCONSISTENT",
  "interpretation_fixed_in_advance": "NEC_FULL / NEC_BULK: in the donors' own forward, the L11 append-span write (its context-read part) is necessary for recognition, not only sufficient for repair in hosts - with M1-M5 a two-directional (interchange) causal role at L11; a failing host's write carries a not-conflict reading of the same context. NOT_NEC: the donor recognises through other paths as well (redundancy); M1-M5 remain sufficiency only. Level S1-S3 boundary: an interchange intervention on natural recognition (the standard's par. 3.3 'local necessity'), not a natural error path in the failing hosts",
  "measures": "C_loss(arm) = share of cells whose patched donor has M <= 0; J_loss(arm) = share of JOINT-donor cells whose patched donor is not JOINT; paired dM_host - dM_ctrl per cell; per-donor majorities",
  "readouts": "M = conflict margin, A = action margin, JOINT = M > 0 and A > 0, on the donor's new arm; baselines = the donor's in-run new capture (bitwise == M1)",
  "reported": "bulk_round_self and bulk_hostmean C_loss / J_loss / median dM (14 rows each); per host; leave one donor group out of each verdict",
  "sets": "all 14 donors are strict recognizers (M > 0); 10 of them are JOINT natively (M1 / K-C captures); C_loss is scored over all cells, J_loss over the cells of the JOINT donors",
  "verdict_bulk": "NEC_BULK: the same rule on bulk_host vs bulk_ctrl",
  "verdict_full": "NEC_FULL iff C_loss(full_host) - C_loss(full_ctrl) >= 0.40 and dM(full_host) < dM(full_ctrl) in >= 75% of cells and in a majority of cells for >= 10 of 14 donors; NOT_NEC_FULL iff the difference < 0.10; else NEC_FULL_PARTIAL"
 },
